# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. Never commit real values.
# A development database with made-up data only. Never the production connection string.
# Either a hosted one, such as Neon (Neon > Connect > pooled connection string):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@ep-<name>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
# and its host name (no user name or password), so the seed may write to it. Never Supabase.
# SEED_ALLOWED_HOST=ep-<name>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech
# Or the local Docker database (npm run db:up), which only exists on your computer:
DATABASE_URL=postgres://fmaw:local@127.0.0.1:54329/fmaw_dev
# Optional: puts the whole site behind HTTP Basic auth (any user name).
# SITE_PASSWORD=
# Password for /admin (any user name). Unset means /admin returns 404.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
